<h2><a id="Presentació" name="Presentació"></a>Presentation and options</h2>

<p>This module calculates statistical data of raster images in which it is possible to choose between three options: The calculation of statistical data of a single raster (monoband or multiband), the calculation of an image with the result of the chosen statistical function in a raster serie and standardizing a raster (monoband or multiband).</p>

<p>For the calculation of statistical data of a single raster, the input file must be an IMG raster file and at least one of the available statistical functions must be selected (depending on the selected treatment of the data). The output file must be an INI file where the result of the different chosen statistical calculations will be written. This option allows doing calculation for all bands of a multiband raster file.</p>
	
<p>For the calculation of an image of the statistics of a raster serie, the input file must be a TXT file with the list of raster files in the IMG format to use for the calculation. There must be at least two raster files to perform the calculation and have the same number of rows and columns. The calculation is done pixel by pixel where for each pixel all the valid values of the pixel that are in the same position in the input rasters are selected and with these values the chosen statistical function is applied and the result is written to the raster output file that must be an IMG raster file.</p>
	
<p>In the option of normalizing a raster, the input file and the output file must be an IMG raster file. This option allows doing this calculation for all bands of a multiband raster file.</p>
	
<p>In order to calculate the frequencies or areas of the different categories of a categorical raster, the Histo module or the query for attributes of the main module of the MiraMon can be used.</p>


